    "result_text": "Done. Build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec \u2014 reject creating an owner when the target city already holds 50+ owners, responding 409 \u2014 maps exactly onto the existing \"unique telephone\" / \"unique household\" reject-check pattern, so I mirrored it as small, self-contained units rather than growing any existing class:\n\n- **`RequireCityCapacity.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners in the request's city (case-insensitive) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new checked exception).\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler.java`** (new) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` via the shared `ProblemDetails` builder, identical in shape to the sibling handlers.\n- **escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `capacity:` step between `household` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nEach new class has no surrounding methods (WMC_other = 0), the one function I wrote is a single simple loop/count with CC \u2248 2, and I edited no existing Java function \u2014 the only touched existing file is the YAML wiring. `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
